<title>FINLAND: NESTE'S GASUM PLANS FIM 50 MLN PIPELINE.</title>
<headline>NESTE'S GASUM PLANS FIM 50 MLN PIPELINE.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Natural gas company Gasum Oy, part of Finnish state-controlled oil and energy group Neste Oy, is planning to build a natural gas pipeline in the Sipoo-Vantaa area in southern Finland, Gasum said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The pipeline would secure the supply of natural gas to the Helsinki capital region, Gasum said in a statement. The cost of the project, due to be completed in October 1998, was forecast at slightly more than 50 million markka, it said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 0 - 680 50 245</p>
